      "message": "this is extremely expensive as it triggers a new SkImage, which in turn makes it un-cachable. So this is triggering texture uploads every frame if the SkImage isn\u0027t already GPU-backed (and if it is maybe copies? dunno). But there\u0027s good news! I think you just want to replace makeShader with makeRawShader which just disables the colorspace handling when you sample from it. As a bonus, makeRawShader is publicly stable ( Android exposes it here: https://developer.android.com/reference/android/graphics/RuntimeShader#setInputBuffer(java.lang.String,%20android.graphics.BitmapShader) )",
